WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.757
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:09.385
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:16.552
Unit twenty-two: It's Time / I'd Rather. Today you will express preferences and say that something should happen now.

4
00:00:16.852 --> 00:00:19.539
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.350
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:25.184
It's time.

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:28.508
It's time means used to say now is the moment.

8
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:30.362
It's time we left.

9
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.765
Your turn. Say: It's time.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.613
It's time.

11
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.514
It's high time.

12
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:43.805
It's high time means stronger; it is past the right time.

13
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.975
It's high time you studied.

14
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:49.445
Your turn. Say: It's high time.

15
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.661
It's high time.

16
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:55.383
I'd rather.

17
00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:58.325
I'd rather means I prefer to.

18
00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:00.301
I'd rather stay in.

19
00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:03.453
Your turn. Say: I'd rather.

20
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.255
I'd rather.

21
00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:08.890
Would rather.

22
00:01:09.883 --> 00:01:12.289
Would rather means the full form of I'd rather.

23
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:14.105
She would rather walk.

24
00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:17.021
Your turn. Say: Would rather.

25
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:20.833
Would rather.

26
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:22.457
Prefer.

27
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.090
Prefer means to like better.

28
00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:26.998
I prefer tea.

29
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:30.015
Your turn. Say: Prefer.

30
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:33.775
Prefer.

31
00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:35.634
Past form.

32
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.136
Past form means a past tense used for an unreal present.

33
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.065
It's time we went.

34
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:45.233
Your turn. Say: Past form.

35
00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.114
Past form.

36
00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:50.851
Present meaning.

37
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.709
Present meaning means a present sense with a past verb.

38
00:01:55.317 --> 00:01:56.562
A present meaning.

39
00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.976
Your turn. Say: Present meaning.

40
00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:03.869
Present meaning.

41
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:05.513
Preference.

42
00:02:06.517 --> 00:02:09.375
Preference means a stronger liking for one choice.

43
00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:11.205
My preference.

44
00:02:11.817 --> 00:02:14.446
Your turn. Say: Preference.

45
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.255
Preference.

46
00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:23.066
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:26.566
Visal, what would you rather do this weekend?

48
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:36.481
I'd rather stay at home than go out. I'd rather is followed by the base verb when the subject is the same. We use than to compare two choices.

49
00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:39.269
What if the subject changes?

50
00:02:40.383 --> 00:02:53.513
We use the past simple with a present meaning: I'd rather you didn't smoke here. It's time we left. It's high time you started working. The past tense shows that the situation is not as we want.

51
00:02:54.617 --> 00:02:55.908
Is it unreal?

52
00:02:57.017 --> 00:03:11.981
Yes. I'd rather you stayed means I want you to stay, though you may not. Compare: I'd rather go (same subject, base verb) and I'd rather you went (different subject, past form). Prefer + -ing is also possible.

53
00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.715
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.766
Grammar focus: It's time plus past; I'd rather plus base verb and past.

55
00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:22.241
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.054
I'd rather stay at home than go out.

57
00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.195
It's time we left.

58
00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:30.071
I'd rather you didn't smoke here.

59
00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:39.691
I'd rather + base verb (same subject). I'd rather + subject + past simple (different subject). It's (high) time + subject + past simple.

60
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.300
Be careful! Don't say: It's time we leave.

61
00:03:45.233 --> 00:03:47.012
Say: It's time we left.

62
00:03:47.312 --> 00:03:48.813
Use the past form.

63
00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.043
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:54.334
Preferences and Moments.

65
00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.225
This weekend I would rather stay at home than go out.

66
00:03:58.233 --> 00:04:01.429
It's time we left; the film starts in ten minutes.

67
00:04:02.433 --> 00:04:05.315
It's high time you started revising for the exam.

68
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.183
I'd rather you didn't smoke in the car.

69
00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.268
I prefer tea, but my preference changes with the weather.

70
00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:17.647
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.483 --> 00:04:19.879
It's time we blank.

72
00:04:20.179 --> 00:04:23.252
A, leave. B, left. C, will leave.

73
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.927
The answer is B: left.

74
00:04:30.083 --> 00:04:32.002
I'd rather blank at home tonight.

75
00:04:32.302 --> 00:04:35.943
A, stay. B, to stay. C, staying.

76
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.314
The answer is A: stay.

77
00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.195
I'd rather you blank here. (a request)

78
00:04:45.495 --> 00:04:49.323
A, don't smoke. B, didn't smoke. C, won't smoke.

79
00:04:52.867 --> 00:04:55.261
The answer is B: didn't smoke.

80
00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:57.720
Which is stronger?

81
00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.114
A, It's time. B, It's high time. C, I'd rather.

82
00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.782
The answer is B: It's high time.

83
00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:11.636
According to the reading, when does the film start?

84
00:05:11.936 --> 00:05:15.543
A, in ten minutes. B, tonight. C, tomorrow.

85
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.250
The answer is A: in ten minutes.

86
00:05:22.467 --> 00:05:25.514
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.187
What would you rather do this weekend?

88
00:05:36.983 --> 00:05:38.600
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:49.450
This weekend I would rather go hiking than stay at home. I'd rather my friends came with me, because it is more fun. It's time we planned a trip, as we haven't travelled for months.

90
00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.319
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:58.747
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and it's time plus past; i'd rather plus base verb and past.

92
00:05:59.047 --> 00:06:03.859
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:06:04.159 --> 00:06:07.426
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:07.726 --> 00:06:10.146
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

